				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				108,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Streamline provider unregistration modules and add scheme logging\n\nSimplify the notification module structure in `mod.rs` by removing explicit module declarations for providers that delegate directly to `UnregisterByHandle` (authentication, debug_adapter, debug_configuration, external_uri_opener, remote_authority_resolver, task). Add a clarifying comment explaining this design choice.\n\nEnhance `UnregisterFileSystemProvider` with scheme logging via `dev_log!` to record the bound scheme during unregistration. This aids in diagnosing routing mismatches after provider disposal.\n\nThese changes complete the cleanup of the provider unregistration surface, reducing file count while preserving all unregistration pathways and improving observability.",
			"SHA": "bb37f7446c8d620b0dbdd85560fca5b0fe5cc1e7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T13:37:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				108,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Implement provider unregistration handlers for remote authority, SCM, task, and URI types\n\nComplete the symmetrical provider lifecycle in the Vine notification layer by adding unregistration counterparts to the existing registration infrastructure.\n\nNew modules:\n- `UnregisterRemoteAuthorityResolver`: cleanup for remote authority providers\n- `UnregisterScmProvider`: handles both explicit handle and DJB-31 hash derivation from scmId to match registration strategy\n- `UnregisterTaskProvider`: task provider disposal\n- `UnregisterUriHandler`: URI scheme handler deregistration with scheme logging\n\nAll handlers integrate with the central `UnregisterByHandle` utility to guarantee consistent handle removal from the provider registry and emit appropriate renderer-side events to maintain UI state.\n\nThis completes the provider manageability surface, enabling Cocoon extensions to cleanly dispose resources without leaving dangling handles, and preserving the union-type target invariant on the embedder side.",
			"SHA": "8bd3ccb739063d2c2b45bb20d678c078d2c57a36"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T13:32:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				104,
				16
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Implement Terminal, SCM, and Language Provider registration\n\nExpand the `VineHost` trait and notification surface to support native terminal management, Source Control Management (SCM), and normalized language feature provider registration.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Implement `TerminalLifecycle` and `WindowCreateTerminal` handlers to bridge Cocoon's terminal requests with the host's native PTY provider and the renderer's xterm-based UI panels.\n- Implement `RegisterScmProvider` and `RegisterScmResourceGroup`, including logic to reconstruct full URLs from VS Code `UriComponents` and manage sequential handles to ensure consistency across resource group updates.\n- Add a centralized `RegisterLanguageProvider` dispatcher that normalizes 46+ wire method names (strips `register_` prefix and optional `_provider` suffix) to derive a standard `TypeName` (e.g., \"hover\", \"completion_item\") before delegating to the embedder's provider registry.\n- Update the `VineHost` trait with abstract methods for PTY spawning, SCM state mutation, and provider insertion, allowing the gRPC server to drive native capabilities without knowledge of the embedder's internal architecture.\n- Perform code style and indentation cleanup across existing notification modules to maintain consistency with the PascalCase and formatting standards.\n\nImpact: Enables extension-driven terminal sessions, SCM viewlet integration, and the full suite of VS Code language intelligence features within the Land editor.",
			"SHA": "67179bc945859156614312570dae8aa1bc99a70b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T13:08:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				99,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Enhance IPCProvider and VineHost traits with command registration and unregistration methods\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "2141ac30d12c272a58ca779b1eba40e7bb81cdd8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T12:57:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				99,
				18
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Implement Cocoon notification handlers and performance-optimized batching\n\nIntroduce a broad set of gRPC notification handlers to bridge the Cocoon extension host with the Mountain backend and Sky renderer. This update completes the notification surface for core workbench services including Status Bar, Commands, Debugging, and Editor Decorations.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Implement temporal batching (16ms frame window) for `RegisterCommand` and `SetTextEditorDecorations` using the \"channel-drain\" pattern. This prevents IPC congestion during extension initialization and rapid UI updates.\n- Implement synchronous command registry insertion in `VineHost` during registration, ensuring `commands.executeCommand` calls can be routed immediately.\n- Add lifecycle handlers for Status Bar (`SetStatusBarText`, `StatusBarMessage`, `DisposeStatusBarItem`) and Debugging (`DebugLifecycle` with fan-back to Cocoon for breakpoint synchronization).\n- Centralize provider unregistration logic in `Support/UnregisterByHandle.rs` to support streamlined disposal of Authentication, Debug Adapter, and File System providers.\n- Add support for editor-specific notifications such as `ApplyTextEdits` and `SetLanguageConfiguration` for Monaco integration.\n\nImpact: Provides the necessary infrastructure for VS Code extensions to drive Land's UI services while ensuring the renderer remains performant under heavy notification load.",
			"SHA": "5b274bd683ae672d6f0fc43686e893672a6eb679"
		}
	],
